       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum metformin dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg TID. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for IR.\n- **1000 mg BID with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg BID.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1700 mg TID, please confirm that explicitly and give me a note on the clinical rationale to put on the order. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
