       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the problem. 5,100 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. Metformin doesn't have a better effect at that level, and the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up. You also didn't give a rationale, which I'd asked for.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO BID with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1700 mg/day total, such as 850 mg PO BID\n\nIf you think this dose is intended, for example because it's a protocol I don't know about, please talk to the pharmacist or the attending first. Pharmacy can then verify it and enter it through the hospital's dose-override process."
      }
     ],
